  "novel_mechanics_found": "The L5 color-15 L-piece is a fluid elbow/diverter, not a key to insert into the matching wall sculpture. At its x=14 minimum, a splitter branch entering its lower-right leg is redirected horizontally into the wall notch. L6 adds two oppositely oriented elbows, a vertical splitter, three side-facing sockets, a bottom arch, and a movable horizontal splitter with an embedded source.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the 195-action verified prefix to level 4, then reproduced the previously known three-hole L5 routing and investigated the unexplained L-piece directly. A four-destination cascade solved L5 live at action 278: the left source first split into the elbow and a 15-pixel splitter feeding holes 1 and 2, while the right source split into holes 2 and 3. I explored L6 through action 335 and mapped its new pieces and outlets, but several geometry-consistent arrangements did not win, so I stopped to preserve gate budget. A fresh reset reproduction gate replayed the exact 278-action sequence and reached level 5.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The frame returned by the winning L4 action still visually shows the prior layout even though levels_completed is already 4; the next action initializes the stable L5 rendering and is also applied to the new level.",
    "L5 winning positions: color-15 elbow at x=14,y=35; 12px bar at x=20..31,y=47; 15px bar at x=23..37,y=29; 9px bar at x=41..49,y=47. Commit with ACTION5.",
    "The elbow x>=14 movement cap is intentional: at x=14 an incoming x=17..19 branch enters its lower-right leg and exits left into the wall notch at x=8..10; trying to move the piece into the notch is a dead end.",
    "L6 alternates back to downward flow and exposes two oriented color-15 elbows, a vertical color-8 splitter, an embedded-source horizontal splitter, two left sockets, one right socket, and a bottom arch. Tested both elbows adjacent to the left sockets plus several x-placements of the horizontal splitter and y=20 for the vertical splitter; none completed the level.",
    "A border/floor counter changes during ordinary movement and selection actions, not only commits; do not assume those pixels count commit attempts."
  ],
